@TID
Feature: a fixture target whose pipeline holds every disposition at once

  A FIXTURE target (NOT under features/) standing in for a consumer whose pipeline exercises all
  four things a step can be. Its ten steps are three the manifest calls non-checks, one running
  the runner it names for the unit tier, two that are the reconciliation and the record it reads,
  and four candidate quality checks — one of them an action rather than a command.

  FOUR FIGURES NOBODY CAN SWAP IS THE WHOLE SHAPE OF IT. Four, one, two and three: no two
  dispositions carry the same count, so a reader that attributed a step to the wrong one reds on
  the figures even where the total would have survived the mistake. Every other @USG fixture has
  at most three of the four dispositions in it, so none of them can hold this claim.

  AND THE ACTION IS AMONG THE CANDIDATES DELIBERATELY. A run:-only reading is the historical shape
  of exactly the fault this target is here to catch, and under the identity it reads as a step
  seen and accounted for as nothing rather than as no evidence at all.

  Rule: a rule holding the target to nothing this axis can cite

    @unit @SCN-TID-001
